           For k = 1 and k = n, the unique state is fixed. Consequently, for every n ≥ 2, the maximum over
           all set partitions of [n] is n − 2.
      (ii) In the dense range n ≥ 2k, a k-block state is recurrent precisely when its first n − k letters form a
           surjective restricted-growth word on all k letters and its final k letters are a permutation of them.
           In the sparse range n ≤ 2k, it is recurrent precisely when its first k letters are 01 · · · (k − 1) and
           its final n − k letters are distinct.
