This entire factor is the directed-cycle chip-firing mechanism already subtracted above. We record its
finite-time lemma because the labelled lift needs an exact entrance bound.
Lemma 2 (queue smoothing). Assume m > 0. If m ≤ k, then every zi is in {0, 1} after at most m − 1
steps. If m ≥ k, then every zi is positive after at most k − 1 steps. The resulting sparse and dense regimes
are forward invariant.
