The terminal k positions first become a permutation at s = k − 1. Therefore (10) has tail n − 2 in the
sparse range and 2k − 2 in the dense range.
   For n ≥ 3, choosing k = n − 1 gives the global value n − 2. At n = 2 both available strata are fixed and
the same formula is zero. This completes the proof.                                                       □

